  "scope": "Selected 4-stage bilateral 3D-printed FDM arm connector architecture (Stages 1-4: Shoulder Pitch-to-Roll, Shoulder Roll-to-Yaw, Upper-Arm Yaw-to-Elbow, Forearm Elbow-to-Wrist) with 34 pressed-in 304 SS compression sleeves per arm (68 bilateral), 4 forearm M3x8 captive-nut hard-shell mounts per arm (8 bilateral = 38 bolted connections/arm, 76 bilateral), full 3D asymmetric edge beveling (r_inner > r_outer), overhauled C-channel Stage 1 bridge with flush 3.00 mm pitch horn hub and zero floating shoulder shell screws, and down-first wrap-around Stage 3 upper-arm routing for easy fabric covering. Physical print, bolt preload retention, cyclic fatigue, and learned-control qualification remain separate.",
